commit d14e04b28153eab5ca3d8f6ea069c4ccec51110c
Author: mac <mac@Hz.local>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 17:18:28 2026 +0000

    S4 phase 2: a private MLX compile directory per evaluation worker; probe p1 failure kept; P218 and P219 accepted
    
    - Probe p1 stopped in evaluation: six workers compiled the same fused CPU
      kernel (nn.relu is an mx.compile function) into the shared cache that a
      reboot had emptied, and collided on one shared library (ld errno 17).
      Reproduced: 23 of 48 runs fail with a shared directory, 0 of 48 with one
      directory per process. Workers now set their own TMPDIR first thing; a
      native test checks that MLX writes the kernels there.
    - P218 (gemini-k7b2): independent NumPy recompute tool, bit-identical on the
      round G records; P219 (gemini-h8f2): reserve and tau = DT boundary tests.
    - The failed probe's report, log and run directory are kept as they are.
    The worker change is not yet reviewed by a non-author.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

